WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.589
The Dogs’ Mind analyses your dog's behaviour. In two minutes I'll show you how it works.

00:00:05.035 --> 00:00:11.980
Tap Log In and choose your profile: Private, if you have one or two dogs. Professional, if you work with canine behaviour.

00:00:12.426 --> 00:00:19.789
To create an account, scroll down to New User and fill in your details: your name, your dog, the country, your email and a password.

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:26.003
If you have an invitation code, type it here. Exactly as it is, with no spaces and no full stop.

00:00:26.448 --> 00:00:32.449
Accept the privacy policy and tap Create my account. You get five hundred free credits, no card needed.

00:00:32.894 --> 00:00:35.377
If you already have an account, you log in here.

00:00:35.823 --> 00:00:40.083
This is the home screen. For a behaviour problem, tap New consultation.

00:00:40.529 --> 00:00:44.064
Niaz asks what you want to do. Let's pick the behaviour problem.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:52.164
First, the dog: name, age, breed, where it lives, how many walks. The more precise you are, the better the analysis.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:59.796
Then the problem: what the dog does, since when, where, and with whom. Here Luna barks and jumps on visitors when the doorbell rings.

00:01:00.242 --> 00:01:04.508
You can see what it costs in credits. Tap Analyse with AI and wait about a minute.

00:01:04.954 --> 00:01:09.354
This is the functional analysis: antecedent, behaviour, consequence.

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:14.000
If you want it in plain words, tap Explain, and Cecilia walks you through it.

00:01:14.446 --> 00:01:16.118
Then tap See Intervention Plan.

00:01:16.563 --> 00:01:20.583
The plan tells you what to do, step by step, with measurable criteria.

00:01:21.029 --> 00:01:24.545
At the bottom, tap Accept intervention, and the case is saved.

00:01:24.991 --> 00:01:30.404
The case goes to your Records: reopen it whenever you like, change its status or download the PDF.

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:32.937
Under each case there's the Daily follow-up.

00:01:33.382 --> 00:01:37.362
Every day it gives you the exercises for today, explained step by step.

00:01:37.808 --> 00:01:41.726
You mark how it went, and the next day's plan takes your answer into account.

00:01:42.171 --> 00:01:45.634
For training: New consultation, then train an exercise.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.847
You set the dog's level, your level, what motivates it and where you train.

00:01:50.292 --> 00:01:53.495
And you write the goal: stay lying down while I open the front door.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.605
You get the training plan, with the sessions to run.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.769
Save it, download it as a PDF, or talk it through with Cecilia.

00:02:01.215 --> 00:02:04.155
For a puppy, the third option: educate and prevent.

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:09.115
It asks for the age in weeks, the origin, the weaning, and what you want to achieve.

00:02:09.561 --> 00:02:13.888
And it gives you the growth plan: which developmental window your puppy is in right now.

00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:16.535
On the home screen there's also Today's walk.

00:02:16.981 --> 00:02:21.521
Share your location, say how active your dog is, and tap Find my three routes.

00:02:21.967 --> 00:02:25.506
It suggests three real routes near you, at the right distance for your dog.

00:02:25.952 --> 00:02:33.266
The Aigents are your consultants. Cecilia is there to help you understand behaviour terms, or something in the plan the app has made for your dog.

00:02:33.712 --> 00:02:42.756
There's also Ale, a vet and trainer. Niaz, for grooming and lifestyle. Katja, for evidence-based nutrition. And Mario, for city life with a dog.

00:02:43.202 --> 00:02:46.806
You type your question and she answers taking your own case into account.

00:02:47.252 --> 00:02:52.012
Credits are topped up in Plans: Basic, Medium, Pro and Max, all monthly.

00:02:52.458 --> 00:02:54.788
And if you have a team code, you enter it here.

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:58.099
Here you can see how many credits each feature costs.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:02.167
That's everything. If something doesn't add up, come back to this video.
